that we're doing is doing something for

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:07.640
our skin as well. So, don't rush and

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:09.120
just go slow and try to feel difference

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.240
between doing that versus doing your

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:13.600
skin care as a task. Habit seven,

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:15.840
protecting your peace like it's your job

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:17.560
because it is, but maybe it's even more

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:19.560
important than your job to be honest.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:21.560
But deciding to do this and exactly what

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:24.400
to do about it is the hard part because

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:26.840
you cannot heal in the same environment

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:28.560
that kept you unwell in the first place.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:30.760
And if your thoughts are making you

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:32.720
unwell, you need different thoughts.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:35.080
This applies to your mental headspace,

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:36.920
it also applies to physical spaces, your

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:39.560
environment. For example, if you get a

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:41.480
text or notification, you're rushing to

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:43.360
respond to it immediately. No, you don't

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:45.480
have to do that. You can always set

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.920
aside a specific time to take care of

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:48.800
that. If you're really not feeling it

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:50.240
right now and you're like, let me just

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:52.600
wallow in my sadness for a little

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:54.160
longer, just go ahead and do that. You

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:55.920
don't have to respond to anything

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:57.600
immediately. But also don't dwell on

00:20:55.920 --> 00:21:00.280
your sadness, please. In fact, most of

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:01.760
the day my phone is on silent mode or on

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.920
focus mode because it's genuinely

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:05.880
something that's super important to me.

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:08.560
And if someone is really trying to reach

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:10.760
me, they can call me. I also set aside

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:13.640
specific times to scroll social media if

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:15.640
I have to. I try to not even do it and I

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:18.920
don't log onto Instagram every day. I

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:20.920
really try to limit myself because

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:23.320
consuming too much content also spikes

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:24.880
your anxiety levels and can make you

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.280
feel worse about yourself. There are a

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.880
lot of subconscious things that we're

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:29.520
doing in the background as we're

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:31.760
scrolling, as we're reading a thousand

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.960
opinions and we have to be very aware of

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:36.640
that as well as what these thoughts are

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:38.520
turning into from our subconscious going

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:40.360
into our consciousness. There's also

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:41.800
other things protecting your capacity

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:43.520
like knowing that there's things that

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:46.120
you have to do, but you haven't done it

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:47.920
yet. Write that down somewhere where you

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:49.240
can keep track of it for later and try

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:50.640
not to let it float around your head too

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:52.200
much because all of the stuff that gets

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.480
floated around your head, you're not

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.840
going to remember all of it and you're

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.480
going to feel even more stressed in

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:58.120
general because you feel like you have

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:59.720
to remember everything. And no matter

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.560
what, there's constantly something that

00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:03.120
you're going to be forgetting. So, I try

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:05.200
to get everything down onto a piece of

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:07.480
paper or onto my notes app, onto to-do

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:09.440
list, anywhere. Get it out of your head

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:11.080
and onto something physical. There's

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:13.520
also something to be said about having

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:15.840
difficult or uncomfortable conversations

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:17.600
and not delaying it. Try and take care

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:19.600
of it as soon as you know you have to do

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:21.520
it and don't let it linger. If someone

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:23.240
comes to me and says, "Hey, we need to

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:24.400
talk." Instead of being like, "Oh my

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:26.760
god, like what do we have to talk

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:28.320
about?" and freaking out for days over

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:30.920
what they want to talk about, let's have

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:32.400
this conversation right now and get it

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:34.280
out of the way because that's three

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:36.600
additional days of you freaking out for

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:38.640
no reason. Let's just get it over with.

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:40.080
It's going to help your stress levels

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:41.840
and you're going to move on for that

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:43.400
much faster, whatever you have to deal

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:45.840
with. You don't have time for that right

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:48.080
now. By not delaying any uncomfortable

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:50.720
situations, this is going to help you

00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:53.000
heal faster. Even just taking an audit

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:54.400
of your current relationships and things

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:56.320
that you feel like you have to do, but

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:58.200
you don't actually want to do, you can

00:22:56.320 --> 00:23:00.840
always back out of things. You can

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:02.600
always say no and say, "Well, I can't

00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:04.760
make it today. This is not the best time

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:06.840
for me right now, and I'm having a

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:08.960
really busy week. And babes, we are

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:10.640
busy. We're working on ourselves, and

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:12.000
we're working on our healing. It's very

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:13.480
important. It's very high on the

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.640
priority list. So, every single

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:17.600
interaction that you have, whether it's

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:20.000
in your inner world or interacting with

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:22.800
the outside world, they're all costing

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:24.760
you something biologically, emotionally,

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:27.440
and energetically. So, chronic

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:29.280
overstimulation and stress levels will

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:31.120
disrupt your healing process and a bunch

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:34.720
of other things as well. So, protecting

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:36.600
your peace is literally non-negotiable.

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:38.760
I have certain hours of the day where

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:40.000
I'm just unreachable, and I try to take

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:42.360
moments where I'm just walking around

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:44.120
the block or going outside onto my

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:45.600
balcony, or if you have a backyard or a

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:47.640
quiet street that you like to walk

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:49.160
around in, don't even think about

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:51.760
bringing a podcast with you. Don't bring

00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:53.520
music. Just be outside and be present

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:55.840
for a little bit. I promise you, even

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:58.600
just trying this out and see if it's for

00:23:55.840 --> 00:24:01.160
you. Like, it is so grounding to unplug

00:23:58.600 --> 00:24:02.960
yourself and just go on a walk. There's

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:04.280
also you know, saying no without

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:06.720
explaining yourself. You can just say

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:09.120
no. Like, no, I can't make it today. I

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:12.120
can't come to your party, unfortunately,

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:14.720
and you don't owe anyone a justification

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:16.040
for why you can't go. You're protecting

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:17.840
your energy, and you don't even have to

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:19.760
tell them that. So, every time you say

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:22.280
yes to something that will cost you your

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:24.640
