00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:59.280
of us are

00:29:57.080 --> 00:30:01.160
quietly sabotaging this process without

00:29:59.280 --> 00:30:03.440
even realizing it like scrolling on our

00:30:01.160 --> 00:30:05.880
phones until we fall asleep, eating too

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:07.520
late, or having super bright lights on

00:30:05.880 --> 00:30:09.240
until the very second but right before

00:30:07.520 --> 00:30:10.480
we go to bed and then we're wondering

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:12.200
why the next morning we felt like we

00:30:10.480 --> 00:30:14.320
just got hit by a truck. Your evening

00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:16.040
routines have to be built intentionally

00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:17.600
in order for us to create all the cues

00:30:16.040 --> 00:30:19.760
for that to happen and nothing about our

00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:21.600
modern day lives will tell us, "Hey,

00:30:19.760 --> 00:30:23.720
it's time for us to start winding down

00:30:21.600 --> 00:30:25.320
and rest." No. Every night before I go

00:30:23.720 --> 00:30:27.080
to bed, at least two hours before, let's

00:30:25.320 --> 00:30:29.600
say if I go to bed at 11, I will start

00:30:27.080 --> 00:30:31.000
my wind down routine at around 9:00 p.m.

00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:32.520
At least one to two hours before my

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:34.840
actual bedtime. And I will make a tea

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:37.440
that's either a chamomile or a

00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:39.600
sleepytime tea or beauty tea and start

00:30:37.440 --> 00:30:41.440
dimming the lights down at least an hour

00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:42.800
before bedtime so that our bodies know,

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:44.400
"Hey, it's actually night time. We can

00:30:42.800 --> 00:30:46.280
go to bed now." Because bright lights

00:30:44.400 --> 00:30:48.880
suppress [music] melatonin. So,

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:52.160
switching to lamps or candles or even a

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:54.840
salt lamp, and your body will read a low

00:30:52.160 --> 00:30:56.840
warm light, not LED fluorescent lights

00:30:54.840 --> 00:30:59.120
right in your face, by the way, but warm

00:30:56.840 --> 00:31:01.160
lights as okay, it's getting dark now.

00:30:59.120 --> 00:31:03.920
It's time to start slowing down and

00:31:01.160 --> 00:31:06.040
getting some rest. So, no screens for

00:31:03.920 --> 00:31:08.080
the last 30 minutes as well. I know, but

00:31:06.040 --> 00:31:09.480
the blue light from your phone tells

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:11.400
your brain that it's still the early

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.800
afternoon, and it will play tricks on

00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:16.560
your body and delay melatonin production

00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:18.520
by up to 2 hours, which is 2 hours of

00:31:16.560 --> 00:31:20.120
sleep quality that you're losing every

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:22.200
single night as long as you're on your

00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:24.320
phone for half an hour before bedtime,

00:31:22.200 --> 00:31:26.240
which is a lot and a very poor return on

00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:28.360
investment, by the way. So, for me,

00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:30.000
ideally, you know, after a certain time,

00:31:28.360 --> 00:31:32.400
whether it's 9:00 p.m. or even sooner

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:34.840
than that, I try to do no phones. It may

00:31:32.400 --> 00:31:36.760
not be every day, but it's whenever I

00:31:34.840 --> 00:31:38.520
can and whenever I remember to do it.

00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:41.120
And if you take magnesium before bed,

00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:43.920
especially magnesium glycinate or

00:31:41.120 --> 00:31:46.080
magnesium L-threonine, it supports deep

00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:47.440
sleep, and it calms nighttime anxiety.

00:31:46.080 --> 00:31:49.480
It's one of the most underrated

00:31:47.440 --> 00:31:50.920
supplements for overall recovery. It

00:31:49.480 --> 00:31:52.800
lowers your stress levels, helps you

00:31:50.920 --> 00:31:55.080
regulate your body better. So, if you're

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:57.000
struggling with winding down, genuinely,

00:31:55.080 --> 00:31:59.400
this is life-changing. I've had times

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:00.880
where I couldn't sleep all night, and I

00:31:59.400 --> 00:32:02.400
would take some magnesium, and then half

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.920
an hour later, I would be asleep.

00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:06.800
Another thing that you can do to replace

00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:08.680
the scrolling is to read a book instead.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:11.400
Your heart rate actually drops

00:32:08.680 --> 00:32:13.400
significantly within just a few minutes

00:32:11.400 --> 00:32:15.840
of reading. It literally takes away your

00:32:13.400 --> 00:32:18.400
stress and one of the fastest ways to

00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:21.240
shift yourself into, "Okay, this is time

00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:23.200
for me to start resting my body." I also

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:24.720
love having a silk pillowcase. I

00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:26.600
recently bought a new one. If you have

00:32:24.720 --> 00:32:28.200
less friction on your skin, on your

00:32:26.600 --> 00:32:30.760
hair, this actually means that you get

00:32:28.200 --> 00:32:32.520
better quality sleep as well, and less

00:32:30.760 --> 00:32:34.440
sleep creases on your face when you wake

00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:37.040
up, your skin won't be so irritated,

00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:38.920
less hair breakage. It is amazing for

00:32:37.040 --> 00:32:40.800
even just your beauty, but also cools

00:32:38.920 --> 00:32:43.080
your head down so that your pillowcase

00:32:40.800 --> 00:32:45.000
is constantly cold and you fall asleep

00:32:43.080 --> 00:32:48.080
faster instead of tossing and turning

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:50.280
all night. So, do your best to be in bed

00:32:48.080 --> 00:32:53.120
with lights out by 11:00. But, if you

00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:55.600
can, do it closer to 10:30 and your body

00:32:53.120 --> 00:32:58.120
will be wired to follow the darkness.

00:32:55.600 --> 00:33:00.000
Habit 10 is the last habit which ties

00:32:58.120 --> 00:33:01.840
everything together and it is so simple

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:04.000
to do. Every night before you go to

00:33:01.840 --> 00:33:07.040
sleep, write down three things that went

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:09.320
well today. Specific wins from the day

00:33:07.040 --> 00:33:11.600
itself and it can be so small, the

00:33:09.320 --> 00:33:13.520
tiniest things like, "I drank eight

00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:15.640
glasses of water like I said I would. I

00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:17.400
went to bed before midnight. I didn't

00:33:15.640 --> 00:33:18.880
reach out for my phone the first thing

00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:20.360
when I woke up this morning." And then I

00:33:18.880 --> 00:33:22.480
went on a walk without listening to a

00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:24.320
podcast or I said no to something that I

00:33:22.480 --> 00:33:26.760
really didn't want to do. Your brain is

00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:28.880
wired to hold on to negative experiences

00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:30.440
more strongly than positive ones. It is

00:33:28.880 --> 00:33:32.160
a survival mechanism because your

00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:34.080
ancestors needed to remember where all

00:33:32.160 --> 00:33:36.000
the threats were, but today, not so

00:33:34.080 --> 00:33:37.800
much. This is a very natural and human

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:40.120
thing, but if we don't actively

00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:42.400
intervene on this survival mechanism,

00:33:40.120 --> 00:33:44.720
you're going to end every day just

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:46.880
replaying scenarios in their head that

00:33:44.720 --> 00:33:48.680
went wrong or didn't even happen and

00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:50.960
you're just, you know, coming up with

00:33:48.680 --> 00:33:53.120
fantasies to stress yourself out.

00:33:50.960 --> 00:33:54.920
Instead of remembering that you did do a

00:33:53.120 --> 00:33:56.280
few things that you're proud of and you

00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:59.240
did do something good for yourself

00:33:56.280 --> 00:34:02.040
today. So, this conscious practice

00:33:59.240 --> 00:34:04.600
trains your mind over time to scan for

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:06.560
evidence of success and progress. Then,

00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:08.919
what ever your brain is looking for, it

00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:11.080
will only find more and more of it. It

00:34:08.919 --> 00:34:12.760
also helps you to close the loop on your

00:34:11.080 --> 00:34:15.000
day. So, instead of your subconscious

00:34:12.760 --> 00:34:16.639
